## How it is linked

The official feeds already use the same IDs. Ingest just keeps them together:

| Layer | Source | What you see |
|---|---|---|
| City map | OpenFreeMap + MapLibre | Streets, river, neighborhoods |
| Trajectories | GTFS `shapes` + `routes` | Colored lines (801 lime, STM green/orange/yellow/blue) |
| Stops | GTFS `stops` | Dots you can tap |
| Schedules | GTFS `stop_times` + calendar | Next passages at that stop |
| Trip | those IDs walked in order | Walk + bus/métros, one transfer if needed |

Same `stop_id` on the map, in the timetable, and in the itinerary. No third-party paywall in the middle.

Feeds in use:

- RTC: [rtcquebec.ca/donnees-ouvertes](https://www.rtcquebec.ca/donnees-ouvertes) (valid 16 Aug to 18 Dec 2026)
- STM: [stm.info developers](https://www.stm.info/fr/a-propos/developpeurs) (valid to 25 Oct 2026)

## What you can do now

Run `npm run dev` and open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).

- Switch **Québec** / **Montréal**
- Search or tap a stop: **Prochains passages**
- **De / Vers** builds a trip and draws it on the map
- Hints: Place D'Youville, Université Laval, Berri-UQAM, McGill

