Apple and Transit bias “the metro product.” Google biases whatever ranks. After a destination from here, Rive now lists marche / vélo / bus / métro and **puts the smallest door-to-door minutes first**. That is Rome2Rio’s job, not Maps’ job. If vélo is 9 and métro is 14, vélo is first. 70 tests, twice.

**2. Official timetable is the source of truth until riders actually agree.**  
Apple/Google silently overwrite the schedule with their crowd. We built the opposite contract: identity-free probes, snap to the official shape, fuse only with enough recent agreeing samples, otherwise **leave GTFS-RT / the published due alone**. Zero users, one junk ping, or a phone in Laval on a Québec shape: no invented bus. That is the only honest public version of “we know where the bus is.”

**3. Here is the connected device, not the map center.**  
Successive finite GPS samples replace here, in time order. Stale and non-finite drops. Plan and next-due reuse that point. Maps does this inside Apple. We have to do it in a static page or “Ici” is a lie.

**4. Watch without their store.**  
Apple Watch + Maps is better if you live in that garden. The free path is still a URL pulse (`watch.html?m=…`) plus `LiveDeparture.remainMinutes`. Empty payload stays on the empty face. Phone can be off. No $99 listing.

**5. What we will never win, and should not try.**  
Look Around, indoor maps, every bus GPS with 10M users, CarPlay, “the” system transit app. If someone only wants a blue dot and a purple line, they should open Maps. Rive is for: **I am not at Youville, I refuse Transit’s paywall, I want the official grid as of this ingest, and I want the shortest mix first.**

